  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nWhen in register-process you will get \"Phone numbers are not authorized to register on this server\", when defining it in \"homeserver.yaml\" as required.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Edit your \"homeserver.yaml\"\r\n2. Uncomment/add \"msisdn\" in Registration-Section:\r\n`\t# Enable registration for new users.\r\n\t\tenable_registration: True\r\n\tregistrations_require_3pid:\r\n  \t\t- email\r\n  \t\t- msisdn\r\n`\r\n\r\n3. Register a new User [Here I used Riot to register a new Account] \r\n3.1 define e-mail, valid phoneNumber, userName and password\r\n3.2 hit register\r\n\r\nWhen processing, you will see in the log-file:\r\n` 14:30:33,187 - synapse.access.http.8008 - 233 - INFO - POST-44- <IP> - 8008 - Received request: POST /_matrix/client/r0/register/msisdn/requestToken\r\n\r\n2019-02-12 14:30:33,188 - synapse.http.server - 85 - INFO - POST-44- <XForwardedForRequest at 0x7f83ae35c160 method='POST' uri='/_matrix/client/r0/register/msisdn/requestToken' clientproto='HTTP/1.0' site=8008> SynapseError: **403 - Phone numbers are not authorized to register on this server**\"`\r\n\r\nI also tried to set \"disable_msisdn_registration: False\" and \r\n\r\n`allowed_local_3pids:\r\n   - medium: msisdn\r\n     pattern: '\\+491907777777'`\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n- **Homeserver**: \r\nmatrix-synapse\r\n\r\n- **Version**: \r\n0.99.0\r\n\r\n- **Install method**: \r\nI installed it via the official package \r\n\r\n- **Platform**: \r\nDebian 9.7",
